<div id="headers" class="sg__header3">Headers</div>
    <p>Header styles are automatically applied to all <span class="pre">&lt;h1&gt;</span> through <span class="pre">&lt;h6&gt;</span> tags. Additionally, you can add header styles using either a helper class or a mixin that passes the tag number as a parameter, e.g. <span class="pre">@include header(1)</span>.</p>
    <div class="row pb-0">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-4">
                    <div class="sg__header4 bp--mobile"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-4">
                    <div class="sg__header4 bp--tablet"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-4">
                    <div class="sg__header4 bp--desktop"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-4 h1--mobile">
                    <div class="h1">H1</div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-4 h1--tablet">
                    <div class="h1">H1</div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-4 h1--desktop">
                    <div class="h1">H1</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 pt-2 pb-3 pt-md-0 pb-md-0">
            <pre><code class='language-markup'><script type="text/plain" class="language-markup"><span class="h1">H1</span></script></code></pre>
            <pre><code class='language-css'><script type="text/plain" class="language-css">.element {@include header(1)}</script></code></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="row">
